WEBVTT

1
00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:21.986
Ben's eyes went wide as he floated into the gym.

2
00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:29.171
Tomorrow was the first day of the Monster Academy pet show, and several monsters were already setting up

3
00:00:29.251 --> 00:00:32.258
exhibits. He went over to look at a fish tank.

4
00:00:32.278 --> 00:00:36.821
"Is that a flying shark?"

5
00:00:37.282 --> 00:00:38.643
he asked a fish monster.

6
00:00:39.423 --> 00:00:42.186
A tiny shark leaped out of the tank and snapped at him.

7
00:00:42.206 --> 00:00:44.507
"Yikes!" Ben jumped back.

8
00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:47.450
"Stay away from that display!"

9
00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.011
the fish monster snapped.

10
00:00:49.031 --> 00:00:51.973
"The show doesn't officially start until tomorrow.

11
00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.255
Can't you see that I'm still setting up?"

12
00:00:54.876 --> 00:00:56.397
"Sorry," Ben said.

13
00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:59.680
"I'm looking for Miss Bungle so I can sign up to volunteer.

14
00:01:00.312 --> 00:01:01.112
Do you know where she is?"

15
00:01:01.132 --> 00:01:04.653
"I think she's at the welcome booth over there."

16
00:01:05.233 --> 00:01:07.954
The fish monster pointed at a spot across the gym.

17
00:01:07.974 --> 00:01:09.175
"Thank you."

18
00:01:09.495 --> 00:01:10.395
Ben headed off.

19
00:01:11.895 --> 00:01:17.097
As he floated along, he saw a two-headed monster peering nervously at a piranha-keet.

20
00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.657
Maybe she'd never seen one before.

21
00:01:20.578 --> 00:01:21.358
Ben grinned.

22
00:01:21.838 --> 00:01:25.339
"She'll see lots more pets when the show officially opens," he thought.

23
00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:28.300
"So will Mayor Hubbletree when he comes to the show.

24
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.320
That should be interesting!"

25
00:01:31.121 --> 00:01:35.542
Ben had always liked piranha-keets, but his family didn't have any pets.

26
00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:40.483
His mother was allergic to dogs, and cats didn't like ghosts.

27
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:44.524
So she said it was best for their family to have no pets at all.

28
00:01:45.925 --> 00:01:48.545
But Ben was hoping that would change this weekend.

29
00:01:49.066 --> 00:01:54.487
Maybe at the Monster Academy pet show, he could finally find a pet that his mother would like.

30
00:01:55.687 --> 00:01:59.657
As he hurried past a training ring, he finally spotted Miss Bungle.

31
00:02:00.198 --> 00:02:04.100
She stood at the welcome booth, talking with Mayor Hubbletree and his wife.

32
00:02:04.721 --> 00:02:05.662
Ben greeted them.

33
00:02:05.682 --> 00:02:09.624
"I wanted to sign up to volunteer at the pet show, Miss Bungle.

34
00:02:10.285 --> 00:02:11.546
Do you still need volunteers?"

35
00:02:11.566 --> 00:02:14.388
"Yes, thank you, Ben!"

36
00:02:14.928 --> 00:02:17.570
Miss Bungle started gathering up some things for him.

37
00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:19.952
"That will be great.

38
00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:24.054
Here's a volunteer badge and a schedule of your duties."

39
00:02:24.755 --> 00:02:25.996
Ben took the bag from her.

40
00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:30.221
"Thanks. I think the pet show is going to be a lot of fun."

41
00:02:30.241 --> 00:02:33.003
"Me too," Miss Bungle said.

42
00:02:33.763 --> 00:02:39.946
But Mayor Hubbletree was rubbing his chin, looking worried as a monster went by with a vampire cat.

43
00:02:43.207 --> 00:02:47.249
"I hope these monster pets are well trained, Miss Bungle.

44
00:02:47.629 --> 00:02:50.871
Are you sure a monster pet show is a good idea?"

45
00:02:51.711 --> 00:02:53.552
"It's a wonderful idea, honey!"

46
00:02:54.024 --> 00:02:55.645
Mrs. Hubbletree patted his arm.

47
00:02:55.905 --> 00:02:59.067
"Monsters love animals just as much as people do.

48
00:02:59.648 --> 00:03:01.609
Besides, what could go wrong?"

49
00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:04.090
"Everything!" the mayor said.

50
00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:07.513
Ben could tell that he had more to say, but Mrs.

51
00:03:07.533 --> 00:03:09.954
Hubbletree shushed him with a finger on her lips.

52
00:03:11.015 --> 00:03:14.197
"Stop worrying," she said in a soothing voice.

53
00:03:14.217 --> 00:03:16.038
"It will be fine."

54
00:03:16.798 --> 00:03:18.880
She turned to Ben and changed the subject.

55
00:03:19.584 --> 00:03:22.407
"I love the pet shop in Monsterville that Mr.

56
00:03:22.507 --> 00:03:24.068
Freaky recommended to me.

57
00:03:24.088 --> 00:03:26.690
I got my rainbow gecko there."

58
00:03:27.951 --> 00:03:31.053
She held up a terrarium with a colorful gecko inside.

59
00:03:31.073 --> 00:03:37.098
"If I hadn't gotten Bowie, I wouldn't have gotten invited to this wonderful monster pet show.

60
00:03:37.519 --> 00:03:39.901
It's going to be such a fabulous weekend!"

61
00:03:39.921 --> 00:03:42.463
Ben peered into the terrarium.

62
00:03:42.983 --> 00:03:45.665
He could see the gecko hiding under a little bridge.

63
00:03:45.685 --> 00:03:48.387
"That's a cool-looking lizard, Mrs.

64
00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:51.153
Hubbletree." The mayor's wife beamed.

65
00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:53.936
"Rainbow geckos are very valuable.

66
00:03:54.356 --> 00:03:56.137
And they're smart," she added.

67
00:03:56.157 --> 00:04:03.323
"I registered Bowie for all three competitions at the show—tricks, obedience, and best pet."

68
00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:06.446
"Good luck," Ben said with a smile.

69
00:04:06.986 --> 00:04:12.551
He couldn't imagine how a gecko could compete in a trick or obedience contest, but he'd never been

70
00:04:12.591 --> 00:04:13.692
to a pet show before.

71
00:04:13.712 --> 00:04:16.754
"Maybe Bowie will win some prizes."

72
00:04:17.775 --> 00:04:18.656
She beamed again.

73
00:04:19.104 --> 00:04:20.024
"I hope so!"

74
00:04:21.365 --> 00:04:24.245
Just then Winnie spotted him and waved him over.

75
00:04:24.265 --> 00:04:25.806
"Hey, Ben!"

76
00:04:26.346 --> 00:04:28.687
She was holding her black kitten, Inky.

77
00:04:28.707 --> 00:04:31.347
"Hi, Winnie!"

78
00:04:32.027 --> 00:04:32.948
Ben smiled.

79
00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:34.308
"What are you doing here?

80
00:04:34.568 --> 00:04:36.389
The real show doesn't start until tomorrow."

81
00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:41.690
"Inky and I are checking out the gym so she's not scared tomorrow," Winnie said.

82
00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:45.911
"I've been training her—I think I'm going to enter her in the tricks competition."

83
00:04:45.931 --> 00:04:48.492
"Awesome!" Ben said.

84
00:04:49.012 --> 00:04:52.914
He tried to pet the kitten, but as usual, Inky hissed at him.

85
00:04:53.814 --> 00:04:54.714
Winnie giggled.

86
00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:57.776
"Inky still doesn't like you."

87
00:04:58.276 --> 00:04:59.156
Ben sighed.

88
00:05:00.357 --> 00:05:02.477
"Cats don't like ghosts, remember?"

89
00:05:03.098 --> 00:05:04.298
Winnie hugged Inky.

90
00:05:04.318 --> 00:05:07.500
"There will be lots of different kinds of pets at the show.

91
00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.961
Maybe you can find one for your family while you're here."

92
00:05:10.981 --> 00:05:14.302
"I was thinking the same thing," Ben said.

93
00:05:14.322 --> 00:05:18.324
"There's just one huge problem—my mom."

94
00:05:19.032 --> 00:05:20.833
"You mean because she's allergic to dogs?"

95
00:05:21.193 --> 00:05:21.954
Winnie asked.

96
00:05:21.974 --> 00:05:24.775
"Yeah, there's that problem," Ben replied.

97
00:05:24.795 --> 00:05:29.218
"But the fact is, she doesn't really like any pets."
